WEBVTT

00:00:04.554 --> 00:00:08.046
We are losing containment
in the starboard nacelle tube.

00:00:08.091 --> 00:00:10.252
Try to get more power
to the field coils.

00:00:10.294 --> 00:00:11.386
Aye, sir.

00:00:11.428 --> 00:00:12.588
Mr. La Forge, report.

00:00:12.629 --> 00:00:15.257
I can't shut down
the plasma injectors.

00:00:15.299 --> 00:00:17.529
Somebody's locked out
the controls.

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:20.798
The plasma venting system
has engaged.

00:00:26.944 --> 00:00:28.775
Two more decks.

00:00:29.913 --> 00:00:31.540
Riker to Bridge.

00:00:31.581 --> 00:00:33.412
We've almost reached
the nacelle tube.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.644
Acknowledged.

00:00:34.685 --> 00:00:36.414
Release the exterior hull plate.

00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:38.182
We may have
to jettison the core.

00:00:38.221 --> 00:00:40.212
Aye, sir.

00:00:44.761 --> 00:00:45.921
What happened?

00:00:45.963 --> 00:00:47.191
He locked out the controls.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:48.788
Before we knew
what was happening

00:00:48.832 --> 00:00:50.299
he stepped up onto the walkway.

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:53.428
See if you can help
shut down the plasma flow.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:56.098
I'm afraid if we try
to get any closer

00:00:56.139 --> 00:00:58.539
he will jump through
the force field.

00:01:09.419 --> 00:01:10.477
Dan...?

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:11.544
It's me.

00:01:11.588 --> 00:01:13.112
It's Will Riker.

00:01:22.933 --> 00:01:25.197
I was here yesterday, remember?

00:01:25.235 --> 00:01:29.296
I didn't want to do it.

00:01:34.811 --> 00:01:40.716
But I saw them
and they laughed at me.

00:01:43.286 --> 00:01:44.913
They laughed.

00:01:44.955 --> 00:01:47.685
Whatever happened,
we can talk about it.

00:01:47.724 --> 00:01:48.918
I want to help.

00:01:49.026 --> 00:01:50.459
Stay away!

00:01:52.763 --> 00:01:54.890
I just want to see your face.

00:01:54.931 --> 00:01:56.398
That's all.

00:01:56.433 --> 00:01:57.957
So we can talk.

00:01:59.503 --> 00:02:03.872
I... know what I have to do.

00:02:05.976 --> 00:02:07.671
Dan, no!

00:02:07.711 --> 00:02:09.178
I have unlocked the controls.

00:02:09.212 --> 00:02:11.203
Shutdown procedure initiated.

00:02:11.248 --> 00:02:13.512
There's still plasma
in the injector.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:14.881
It will take time to vent off.

00:02:14.951 --> 00:02:16.714
Tell me what happened.

00:02:16.753 --> 00:02:18.345
Maybe I can help.

00:02:18.388 --> 00:02:21.414
I know what I have to do.

00:02:58.895 --> 00:03:03.229
Space, the final frontier.

00:03:03.266 --> 00:03:07.100
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:03:07.137 --> 00:03:09.105
Its continuing mission...

00:03:09.139 --> 00:03:13.075
to explore strange new worlds

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:17.547
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:03:17.581 --> 00:03:22.416
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:04:23.313 --> 00:04:26.077
A few more seconds,
I could have saved his life.

00:04:26.116 --> 00:04:28.414
Commander, you did
everything you could.

00:04:28.451 --> 00:04:30.442
It was not your fault.

00:04:32.455 --> 00:04:34.286
It was strange.

00:04:34.324 --> 00:04:36.884
I felt as if he didn't even
recognize me...

00:04:36.993 --> 00:04:39.723
even though I was with him
just the other day

00:04:39.763 --> 00:04:41.731
when I supervised
the tube refit.

00:04:41.765 --> 00:04:43.130
How did he seem then?

00:04:43.166 --> 00:04:44.565
Fine.

00:04:44.601 --> 00:04:47.570
I complimented him
on getting the refit done

00:04:47.604 --> 00:04:49.401
faster than expected.

00:04:49.439 --> 00:04:51.805
He was pleased
that I had noticed.

00:04:51.841 --> 00:04:54.275
I met with him
about six weeks ago

00:04:54.311 --> 00:04:56.370
during the crew evaluations.

00:04:56.413 --> 00:04:58.005
He was very positive.

00:04:58.048 --> 00:04:59.913
He was looking forward
to being posted

00:05:00.016 --> 00:05:01.278
to the nacelle tube.

00:05:01.318 --> 00:05:03.081
He was a good officer

00:05:03.119 --> 00:05:05.986
with a fine career ahead of him.

00:05:06.022 --> 00:05:08.786
I don't understand
why he wanted...

00:05:13.563 --> 00:05:16.361
In my years
as a Starfleet Captain

00:05:16.399 --> 00:05:19.163
I have had to notify
many parents

00:05:19.202 --> 00:05:22.467
of the loss of loved ones,
but never before to suicide.

00:05:22.505 --> 00:05:26.134
I would like to be able to offer
Lieutenant Kwan's parents

00:05:26.176 --> 00:05:28.508
some explanation
of what happened

00:05:28.545 --> 00:05:31.378
to try to help them
make sense of this.

00:05:31.414 --> 00:05:36.317
Well, maybe he left, um...
a message of some kind

00:05:36.353 --> 00:05:38.344
explaining why he did it.

00:05:38.388 --> 00:05:40.117
I would like the two of you

00:05:40.156 --> 00:05:42.420
to piece together a picture
of his last few days.

00:05:42.459 --> 00:05:43.983
If he made any personal logs

00:05:44.027 --> 00:05:46.325
it might be helpful
to look through them.

00:05:46.363 --> 00:05:48.024
You're authorized to do so.

00:05:51.935 --> 00:05:53.630
La Forge to Captain.

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:54.830
Go ahead.

00:05:54.871 --> 00:05:57.499
I've just finished
my damage assessment.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.405
We should be able to get
underway

00:05:59.442 --> 00:06:00.841
I'd say within the hour.

00:06:00.877 --> 00:06:02.538
Mr. La Forge,
The medical situation

00:06:02.579 --> 00:06:03.841
on Barson II has worsened.

00:06:03.913 --> 00:06:05.540
Starfleet has given us
permission

00:06:05.582 --> 00:06:08.813
to exceed warp speed limitations
so as to get back on schedule.

00:06:08.852 --> 00:06:11.821
We'll be able to give you
warp eight if we need it.

00:06:11.855 --> 00:06:13.083
Acknowledged.

00:06:13.123 --> 00:06:14.750
Geordi...

00:06:14.791 --> 00:06:16.088
would you agree

00:06:16.126 --> 00:06:18.594
that the instinct
for self-preservation

00:06:18.628 --> 00:06:20.528
is shared by most life-forms?

00:06:20.563 --> 00:06:23.760
I'd say it's probably
the most basic instinct, Data.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:25.267
That being the case

00:06:25.302 --> 00:06:27.429
I find it difficult
to understand

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:29.870
why someone would
deliberately terminate

00:06:29.973 --> 00:06:31.372
their own existence.

00:06:32.976 --> 00:06:34.307
I don't know, Data.

00:06:34.344 --> 00:06:37.177
All I can think is
that maybe Lieutenant Kwan

00:06:37.213 --> 00:06:40.478
felt that there was something...
wrong with his life.

00:06:40.517 --> 00:06:43.281
Something that he felt
powerless to fix.

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:44.480
Hmm...

00:06:44.521 --> 00:06:46.512
I believe I understand.

00:06:46.556 --> 00:06:48.683
I have been
in a similar situation.

00:06:51.661 --> 00:06:52.958
Really?

00:06:54.331 --> 00:06:56.993
The first months
following my activation

00:06:57.033 --> 00:06:59.058
were a difficult period for me.

00:06:59.102 --> 00:07:00.535
There were many problems

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:02.731
associated
with my becoming sentient.

00:07:02.772 --> 00:07:05.502
Because your neural net
was still forming.

00:07:05.542 --> 00:07:06.839
Mm-hmm.

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:11.347
As I acquired new skills,
neural pathways would form

00:07:11.381 --> 00:07:13.849
replacing other,
less complex, pathways.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:17.044
It was very... disorienting.

00:07:17.087 --> 00:07:18.349
I bet.

00:07:18.388 --> 00:07:20.788
As my systems grew
in complexity

00:07:20.824 --> 00:07:22.849
it became
increasingly difficult

00:07:22.959 --> 00:07:24.551
to integrate new pathways

00:07:24.594 --> 00:07:26.562
into my existing neural net.

00:07:26.596 --> 00:07:29.121
The probability
of cascade failure grew

00:07:29.165 --> 00:07:30.860
with each additional pathway.

00:07:30.967 --> 00:07:32.662
I came to the conclusion

00:07:32.702 --> 00:07:35.034
it would be safer, and easier

00:07:35.071 --> 00:07:37.301
to shut myself down
and start again.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:38.500
Yeah, but if you had done that

00:07:38.541 --> 00:07:40.372
you wouldn't have remembered
any of the things

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:41.434
that had happened to you.

00:07:41.478 --> 00:07:43.446
In a way...

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:46.244
it would have been like
committing suicide.

00:07:46.282 --> 00:07:49.445
So what did you do?

00:07:49.486 --> 00:07:51.613
I decided against the procedure.

00:07:51.654 --> 00:07:53.019
I chose, instead

00:07:53.056 --> 00:07:55.786
to treat the problems
I was having with my systems

00:07:55.825 --> 00:07:57.224
as challenges to overcome

00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:59.228
rather than obstacles
to be avoided.

00:07:59.262 --> 00:08:02.356
That's a great way
to look at it, Data.

00:08:02.399 --> 00:08:05.232
I only wish Lieutenant
Kwan had been able

00:08:05.268 --> 00:08:08.135
to look at his problems
the same way.

00:08:15.545 --> 00:08:17.308
This is a Napean design.

00:08:17.347 --> 00:08:19.076
His mother is Napean.

00:08:19.115 --> 00:08:20.776
His father is human.

00:08:22.185 --> 00:08:24.085
It all looks so normal.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:26.179
For some reason,
I half expected

00:08:26.222 --> 00:08:27.712
the place to be a mess.

00:08:27.757 --> 00:08:28.849
Yes.

00:08:28.925 --> 00:08:31.291
It is strange to think
that someone

00:08:31.327 --> 00:08:33.818
could have considered
ending his life

00:08:33.863 --> 00:08:35.854
and yet give no outward sign.

00:08:35.932 --> 00:08:39.265
Just before he jumped,
he seemed almost... calm.

00:08:39.302 --> 00:08:41.770
Well, he must have been
in a lot of pain

00:08:41.805 --> 00:08:43.830
to do what he did.

00:08:43.873 --> 00:08:47.172
It could be that the prospect
of ending the pain

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:49.303
felt like a great relief.

00:08:52.148 --> 00:08:54.343
This is Ensign Calloway,
isn't it?

00:08:54.384 --> 00:08:55.510
Yes.

00:08:55.552 --> 00:08:57.884
She is a medical technician
in Sick Bay.

00:08:57.954 --> 00:09:00.889
It's always hard to lose
someone you care about

00:09:00.957 --> 00:09:03.221
but to lose them like this...

00:09:03.259 --> 00:09:05.693
We should check
his personal logs.

00:09:13.169 --> 00:09:14.727
This is his last entry.

00:09:14.771 --> 00:09:17.672
He made it before going
on duty this morning.

00:09:17.707 --> 00:09:21.837
Personal Log, Stardate 47622.1.

00:09:21.878 --> 00:09:24.312
We finally finished the nacelle
tube refit last night.

00:09:24.347 --> 00:09:27.839
After pulling
two double shifts in a row

00:09:27.884 --> 00:09:31.149
I'm really looking forward to
spending some time with Maddy.

00:09:32.188 --> 00:09:34.247
Ensign Calloway.

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:36.087
That doesn't sound like a man

00:09:36.125 --> 00:09:38.559
who's planning
on taking his own life.

00:09:38.595 --> 00:09:41.564
No. No, it does not.

00:09:53.309 --> 00:09:55.743
I can't believe
he's really gone.

00:09:58.114 --> 00:10:00.548
I keep thinking
he's going to show up

00:10:00.583 --> 00:10:02.210
and tell me there's been

00:10:02.252 --> 00:10:04.846
some kind of terrible
misunderstanding.

00:10:04.888 --> 00:10:07.015
I thought you might
like to know

00:10:07.056 --> 00:10:08.751
that in his personal logs

00:10:08.791 --> 00:10:11.089
Dan talked about you
a great deal.

00:10:11.127 --> 00:10:12.890
He loved you very much.

00:10:12.929 --> 00:10:15.227
If that's true...

00:10:15.265 --> 00:10:18.029
then how could he
leave me like this?

00:10:18.067 --> 00:10:19.796
That's what I'm trying
to find out.

00:10:19.836 --> 00:10:21.531
I know it's hard
to talk right now

00:10:21.571 --> 00:10:22.902
but it would be very helpful

00:10:23.006 --> 00:10:25.270
if you could tell me
a few things about him.

00:10:26.843 --> 00:10:28.902
When was the last time
you saw him?

00:10:29.012 --> 00:10:30.309
Two nights ago.

00:10:30.346 --> 00:10:33.509
We were planning our next
shore leave together.

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:36.212
Did he mention anything
that had happened recently

00:10:36.252 --> 00:10:38.117
anything that might
have upset him?

00:10:38.154 --> 00:10:40.122
No, not really.

00:10:40.156 --> 00:10:43.819
He did say something about work,
about Lieutenant Nara

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:45.919
but it wasn't anything serious.

00:10:46.029 --> 00:10:49.624
Nara... she's his superior
in the nacelle tube.

00:10:49.666 --> 00:10:51.634
Yes.

00:10:51.668 --> 00:10:54.364
Dan sensed that she...

00:10:54.404 --> 00:10:57.066
well, that she felt threatened
by him...

00:10:57.106 --> 00:10:59.939
that she thought he was after
her position.

00:10:59.976 --> 00:11:02.467
Was he prone to mood swings
or depression?

00:11:02.512 --> 00:11:08.747
No, but he was very sensitive
to other people's moods.

00:11:08.785 --> 00:11:10.184
He used to look at me

00:11:10.219 --> 00:11:12.653
and know exactly
what I was feeling.

00:11:12.689 --> 00:11:14.714
I always loved that about him.

00:11:14.757 --> 00:11:17.248
Well, Napeans
are partially empathetic.

00:11:17.293 --> 00:11:20.729
He may have inherited
some of his mother's abilities.

00:11:20.763 --> 00:11:23.527
He used to tease me
that when I met her

00:11:23.566 --> 00:11:26.558
I wouldn't be able
to get away with anything.

00:11:28.438 --> 00:11:31.532
Dan and I knew each other
for over two years

00:11:31.574 --> 00:11:35.169
but we didn't get together
until a few months ago.

00:11:35.211 --> 00:11:36.872
We took it slow.

00:11:36.913 --> 00:11:39.677
We thought we had
all the time in the world.

00:11:39.716 --> 00:11:44.653
Something must have happened
to him, Counselor...

00:11:44.687 --> 00:11:47.656
something terrible...
because it's not like Dan

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:49.419
to take his own life.

00:11:49.459 --> 00:11:50.892
I understand.

00:11:50.927 --> 00:11:52.656
Please...

00:11:52.695 --> 00:11:54.560
find out what it was.

00:12:09.378 --> 00:12:11.073
Can I help you?

00:12:11.113 --> 00:12:13.013
Oh, I didn't see you there.

00:12:13.048 --> 00:12:15.482
You're Lieutenant Nara,
aren't you?

00:12:15.517 --> 00:12:17.508
Can I do something
for you, Counselor?

00:12:17.553 --> 00:12:20.818
I'm investigating
Lieutenant Kwan's death.

00:12:20.856 --> 00:12:23.120
I just wanted to look around.

00:12:23.158 --> 00:12:25.820
It's such a shame.

00:12:25.861 --> 00:12:27.692
He was a good man.

00:12:29.598 --> 00:12:33.295
Did you notice any change
in his behavior recently?

00:12:33.335 --> 00:12:35.701
No.

00:12:35.737 --> 00:12:38.900
I've been going over
the last few days in my mind

00:12:39.007 --> 00:12:41.908
trying to see if I...

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:46.003
if I missed any warning signs.

00:12:46.048 --> 00:12:49.017
It's as if something inside him
just snapped.

00:12:49.051 --> 00:12:51.019
How was his job performance?

00:12:51.053 --> 00:12:52.486
Excellent.

00:12:52.521 --> 00:12:54.216
He knew this ship better
than most people

00:12:54.256 --> 00:12:55.746
probably
because he helped build it

00:12:55.791 --> 00:12:57.281
back at Utopia Planitia.

00:12:57.326 --> 00:12:59.886
Did he get along
with his coworkers?

00:12:59.928 --> 00:13:02.624
He was ambitious.

00:13:02.664 --> 00:13:04.495
He came in here with all sorts
of new ideas

00:13:04.533 --> 00:13:05.591
about how to do things...

00:13:05.634 --> 00:13:07.431
some of them very good ideas.

00:13:07.469 --> 00:13:08.834
But not all?

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:10.599
No.

00:13:10.639 --> 00:13:14.302
But after he settled in,
we got along fine.

00:13:15.677 --> 00:13:16.871
Excuse me a minute.

00:13:16.979 --> 00:13:18.708
Feel free to look around.

00:13:18.747 --> 00:13:21.875
Where was Lieutenant Kwan's
station?

00:13:21.917 --> 00:13:23.475
Right there.

00:14:27.182 --> 00:14:28.479
Are you all right?

00:14:31.486 --> 00:14:33.044
I don't know.

00:14:42.898 --> 00:14:44.991
I don't know how to describe it.

00:14:45.033 --> 00:14:48.059
I was suddenly overwhelmed
by a flood of emotions...

00:14:48.103 --> 00:14:51.072
fear, rage, panic...

00:14:51.106 --> 00:14:54.371
and the sensations didn't seem
to be coming from any person.

00:14:54.409 --> 00:14:56.309
They were just there
in the room.

00:14:56.345 --> 00:14:57.835
Well, then whose emotions
were they?

00:14:57.879 --> 00:14:59.312
I thought you said
you were alone.

00:14:59.348 --> 00:15:01.646
I was.

00:15:01.683 --> 00:15:03.116
I scanned the area.

00:15:03.151 --> 00:15:05.381
I found no anomalous readings.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:07.445
How could you get
an empathic impression

00:15:07.489 --> 00:15:09.047
from an empty room?

00:15:09.091 --> 00:15:10.149
I don't know.

00:15:10.192 --> 00:15:11.489
Could the fact
that Lieutenant Kwan

00:15:11.526 --> 00:15:13.494
was partially empathic
have anything to do with it?

00:15:13.528 --> 00:15:14.552
What do you mean?

00:15:14.596 --> 00:15:15.654
I'm not sure

00:15:15.697 --> 00:15:17.790
but certainly
the feelings Troi described

00:15:17.833 --> 00:15:19.767
are consistent with suicide.

00:15:19.801 --> 00:15:23.134
Could his death have left
some sort of empathic echo?

00:15:23.171 --> 00:15:25.196
I don't see how

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:27.800
but if I went back
to the nacelle tube

00:15:27.843 --> 00:15:31.210
I might get a better sense
of what I experienced.

00:15:31.246 --> 00:15:32.736
I don't think I'd recommend
that right now.

00:15:32.781 --> 00:15:35.147
You're showing elevated levels
of psilosynine.

00:15:35.183 --> 00:15:37.151
Psilosynine?

00:15:37.185 --> 00:15:40.177
It's a neurotransmitter
involved in telepathy.

00:15:40.222 --> 00:15:42.247
The experience overwhelmed you
the first time.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:43.279
I think you should wait

00:15:43.325 --> 00:15:44.883
until your levels
return to normal.

00:15:44.993 --> 00:15:46.893
How long?

00:15:46.928 --> 00:15:48.020
Three, maybe four hours.

00:15:50.265 --> 00:15:52.563
This time,
I want someone with you.

00:15:52.601 --> 00:15:54.762
I shall accompany you,
Counselor.

00:15:57.139 --> 00:16:01.371
Captain's Log, Stardate 47623.2.

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:05.107
We've arrived at Starbase 328
on schedule.

00:16:05.147 --> 00:16:08.139
After taking aboard
medical supplies

00:16:08.183 --> 00:16:10.617
we will depart for Barson II.

00:16:12.154 --> 00:16:13.348
Come in.

00:16:14.556 --> 00:16:15.523
Hello, Worf.

00:16:15.557 --> 00:16:16.854
Counselor.

00:16:16.892 --> 00:16:20.521
Have you found anything
in Lieutenant Kwan's logs?

00:16:20.562 --> 00:16:22.359
Everything I've read

00:16:22.397 --> 00:16:24.991
suggests that he was
well-adjusted

00:16:25.033 --> 00:16:26.398
and optimistic.

00:16:26.435 --> 00:16:28.869
It just doesn't make any sense.

00:16:28.904 --> 00:16:30.838
Can I get you anything?

00:16:30.872 --> 00:16:33.067
No. No, nothing.

00:16:33.108 --> 00:16:35.076
Yridian tea.

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:41.413
I've been thinking
about what happened to me

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:42.883
in the nacelle tube...

00:16:42.918 --> 00:16:49.482
whether it was an empathic echo
left by Kwan's death.

00:16:49.524 --> 00:16:51.822
In the past,
have your empathic experiences

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:54.920
always involved the physical
presence of another person?

00:16:56.198 --> 00:16:57.859
All the ones I'm sure of, yes.

00:16:57.899 --> 00:17:00.060
What do you mean, "sure of"?

00:17:01.937 --> 00:17:04.997
Well, when I was a little girl

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:08.066
my grandfather used to tell me
stories by the fire.

00:17:08.109 --> 00:17:09.804
I would close my eyes

00:17:09.845 --> 00:17:13.110
and listen to his mind
for hours on end.

00:17:13.148 --> 00:17:16.311
He would tell you
these stories telepathically?

00:17:16.351 --> 00:17:18.819
My grandfather rarely spoke.

00:17:18.854 --> 00:17:21.687
He said that was
for off-worlders

00:17:21.723 --> 00:17:25.022
and people
who didn't know any better.

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:28.496
Now, the only time
I can remember his stories

00:17:28.530 --> 00:17:31.863
is when I go home
and sit by the fireplace.

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:34.869
Sometimes, when I'm alone there

00:17:34.903 --> 00:17:38.600
it's almost as if I can hear
his voice inside my head.

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:43.270
Yes. Yes, I, too,
have sought visions in fire.

00:17:43.311 --> 00:17:47.008
I can't explain it,
but it feels real to me.

00:17:47.048 --> 00:17:50.745
Just like what happened
in the nacelle tube.

00:17:50.785 --> 00:17:54.380
There are things
we do not understand

00:17:54.422 --> 00:17:57.084
yet they exist nonetheless.

00:18:02.697 --> 00:18:05.165
Perhaps I should let you
get some rest.

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:06.497
Oh, it's all right.

00:18:06.535 --> 00:18:09.129
No. If you will excuse me,
Counselor.

00:18:29.958 --> 00:18:32.119
I'll be right back.

00:18:34.396 --> 00:18:35.522
Mr. Worf.

00:18:35.564 --> 00:18:36.861
Commander.

00:18:36.898 --> 00:18:38.126
Two Til'amin froths, please.

00:18:38.166 --> 00:18:39.224
Yes, sir.

00:18:45.907 --> 00:18:49.536
Lieutenant Corell seems to be
enjoying your company.

00:18:49.578 --> 00:18:50.875
I'd like to think so.

00:18:50.912 --> 00:18:53.904
Are you involved with her?

00:18:55.917 --> 00:18:57.111
I'm not sure yet.

00:18:57.152 --> 00:18:59.313
Why, are you interested in her?

00:18:59.354 --> 00:19:00.378
No, no.

00:19:00.422 --> 00:19:02.549
But, if I were,
I would, of course

00:19:02.591 --> 00:19:04.491
discuss the situation with you

00:19:04.526 --> 00:19:06.391
before proceeding further.

00:19:06.428 --> 00:19:07.520
I appreciate it

00:19:07.562 --> 00:19:09.359
but that really wouldn't
have been necessary.

00:19:09.397 --> 00:19:10.796
I mean, I would
never want to come

00:19:10.832 --> 00:19:12.823
between you and someone
you are involved with

00:19:12.901 --> 00:19:14.835
or had ever had been
involved with.

00:19:14.869 --> 00:19:18.566
Is there someone in particular
that you're talking about?

00:19:18.607 --> 00:19:19.574
No.

00:19:19.608 --> 00:19:21.371
Is there someone in particular

00:19:21.409 --> 00:19:23.843
you would rather I not
be involved with?

00:19:23.878 --> 00:19:26.278
Mr. Worf, you sound like a man
who's asking his friend

00:19:26.314 --> 00:19:27.838
if he can start dating
his sister.

00:19:27.882 --> 00:19:30.180
No, no, I was merely...

00:19:30.218 --> 00:19:31.207
Never mind.

00:19:31.252 --> 00:19:32.719
Excuse me, sir.

00:20:09.291 --> 00:20:11.486
Could you open this door for me?

00:20:11.526 --> 00:20:13.790
Yes, but only for a short time.

00:20:13.829 --> 00:20:14.887
After 90 seconds

00:20:14.996 --> 00:20:17.624
the plasma venting system
will engage

00:20:17.666 --> 00:20:20.635
to prevent degradation
of the force field.

00:20:20.669 --> 00:20:22.569
I just want
to take a quick look.

00:20:22.604 --> 00:20:25.129
May I ask
what you're looking for?

00:20:25.173 --> 00:20:27.869
I'm not sure.

00:20:35.183 --> 00:20:40.211
Warning. Plasma venting system
will engage in 90 seconds.

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:42.852
No, no!

00:20:42.891 --> 00:20:45.086
No, please!

00:20:45.126 --> 00:20:46.650
Please, please!

00:20:46.695 --> 00:20:48.526
No! Don't!

00:20:48.563 --> 00:20:49.587
No!

00:20:50.966 --> 00:20:56.962
Warning. Plasma venting system
will engage in 80 seconds.

00:21:07.582 --> 00:21:09.413
Worf?

00:21:26.268 --> 00:21:28.259
Worf?

00:22:11.313 --> 00:22:14.077
Counselor... are you all right?

00:22:20.422 --> 00:22:22.413
Let's get out of here.

00:22:31.633 --> 00:22:33.328
Do you remember anything else?

00:22:33.368 --> 00:22:34.835
Yes, I think I do.

00:22:34.869 --> 00:22:37.303
There was a tool crate
on the floor.

00:22:37.339 --> 00:22:40.069
It was labeled
"Utopia Planitia."

00:22:40.108 --> 00:22:43.566
The shipyard where
the Enterprise was built.

00:22:43.612 --> 00:22:48.572
Clearly, this was much more
than an empathic echo.

00:22:48.617 --> 00:22:51.643
It seems that you were actually
seeing something that happened

00:22:51.686 --> 00:22:53.449
in the control room
eight years ago.

00:22:53.488 --> 00:22:56.480
Everyone was looking
directly at me

00:22:56.524 --> 00:22:57.650
but it was as though

00:22:57.692 --> 00:23:00.024
I was seeing
through someone else's eyes.

00:23:00.061 --> 00:23:02.427
Lieutenant Kwan
was partially empathic.

00:23:02.464 --> 00:23:04.557
Maybe you were seeing it
through his eyes.

00:23:04.599 --> 00:23:08.000
It's possible, but I don't see
how it could have happened.

00:23:08.036 --> 00:23:10.869
Well, putting that on one side
for the moment

00:23:10.905 --> 00:23:14.705
let's assume that by some
inexplicable phenomenon

00:23:14.743 --> 00:23:16.370
you witnessed an event

00:23:16.411 --> 00:23:18.879
that occurred
to Lieutenant Kwan.

00:23:18.980 --> 00:23:23.076
Those faces that you saw...
did you recognize any of them?

00:23:23.118 --> 00:23:27.646
I've never seen the woman before
or the man who was with her.

00:23:27.689 --> 00:23:30.886
But there was
someone else there...

00:23:30.992 --> 00:23:33.085
a man.

00:23:33.128 --> 00:23:38.031
He was staring at me
in the most peculiar way.

00:23:38.066 --> 00:23:44.562
I think he had reddish hair
and he did seem familiar to me.

00:23:44.606 --> 00:23:46.574
But it's all so hazy.

00:23:46.608 --> 00:23:49.600
It's like trying
to remember a dream.

00:23:49.644 --> 00:23:53.808
There was a woman
who was frightened

00:23:53.848 --> 00:23:56.339
and then you saw her again,
laughing

00:23:56.384 --> 00:23:58.409
presumably at Lieutenant Kwan.

00:23:58.453 --> 00:23:59.750
What does it all mean?

00:23:59.788 --> 00:24:00.777
I don't know

00:24:00.822 --> 00:24:02.687
but something terrible
happened in that room.

00:24:02.724 --> 00:24:03.850
I felt it.

00:24:03.925 --> 00:24:05.153
Counselor, I want you to look

00:24:05.193 --> 00:24:07.286
through the personnel
files of Utopia Planitia.

00:24:07.328 --> 00:24:09.489
See if you recognize
any of those faces.

00:24:09.531 --> 00:24:11.431
If only I could go back
into the control room

00:24:11.466 --> 00:24:13.866
without being overwhelmed
by the experience.

00:24:13.968 --> 00:24:15.993
It might help me
remember some detail

00:24:16.037 --> 00:24:17.368
that might be relevant.

00:24:17.405 --> 00:24:18.997
I could give you

00:24:19.040 --> 00:24:20.632
an inhibitor
that would slow down

00:24:20.675 --> 00:24:22.540
the brain's production
of psilosynine.

00:24:22.577 --> 00:24:25.273
That might be able to suppress
your empathic abilities

00:24:25.313 --> 00:24:27.304
and make the experience
more manageable.

00:24:27.348 --> 00:24:30.215
It would take about 16 hours
to synthesize the inhibitor.

00:24:30.251 --> 00:24:32.151
I'd like to try that.

00:24:32.187 --> 00:24:33.916
Very well, Counselor.

00:24:40.128 --> 00:24:42.096
I apologize for being late.

00:24:42.130 --> 00:24:45.566
The viral medicines we are
transporting to Barson II

00:24:45.600 --> 00:24:47.727
require special
security measures

00:24:47.769 --> 00:24:50.237
to insure they are
properly contained.

00:24:50.271 --> 00:24:51.898
Have you found anything?

00:24:51.973 --> 00:24:53.235
No.

00:24:53.274 --> 00:24:56.835
There were literally
thousands of people involved

00:24:56.878 --> 00:24:58.937
in building the Enterprise.

00:25:00.615 --> 00:25:04.517
Perhaps you should try to narrow
the search parameters.

00:25:04.552 --> 00:25:05.849
I think I have.

00:25:05.887 --> 00:25:07.616
The man who looked
familiar to me

00:25:07.655 --> 00:25:09.850
may have served
on board the Enterprise

00:25:09.924 --> 00:25:11.391
in the last seven years

00:25:11.426 --> 00:25:14.452
so I've asked the computer
to limit its search

00:25:14.496 --> 00:25:17.363
to personnel who served
at Utopia Planitia

00:25:17.398 --> 00:25:18.797
and on the Enterprise.

00:25:18.833 --> 00:25:23.532
Ensign Salvatore...
he transferred over a year ago.

00:25:23.571 --> 00:25:27.200
Lieutenant Ziff...
she's in quantum mechanics.

00:25:28.877 --> 00:25:30.674
That's him.

00:25:30.712 --> 00:25:33.203
Lieutenant Walter Pierce.

00:25:33.248 --> 00:25:34.476
I remember now.

00:25:34.516 --> 00:25:37.076
He came on board
about six months ago.

00:25:37.118 --> 00:25:39.109
I think he's in Engineering.

00:25:46.427 --> 00:25:50.386
You were Lieutenant Kwan's
supervisor at Utopia Planitia.

00:25:50.431 --> 00:25:51.489
That's right.

00:25:51.533 --> 00:25:53.899
I was sorry
to hear what happened.

00:25:53.935 --> 00:25:57.393
Did you ever spend time
in the nacelle control room

00:25:57.438 --> 00:25:59.702
while it was under construction?

00:25:59.741 --> 00:26:01.902
I worked all over the ship.

00:26:01.943 --> 00:26:04.969
In fact, I remember
running a power conduit

00:26:05.013 --> 00:26:06.981
right behind this wall, here.

00:26:07.015 --> 00:26:09.415
Were you ever
in the nacelle room

00:26:09.450 --> 00:26:10.974
at the same time
as Lieutenant Kwan?

00:26:11.019 --> 00:26:12.509
It was a long time ago.

00:26:12.554 --> 00:26:15.216
People were working
all over the place.

00:26:15.256 --> 00:26:16.848
So you do not remember?

00:26:16.891 --> 00:26:18.791
I'm sorry, I don't.

00:26:20.562 --> 00:26:24.965
Do you recall if anything
unusual happened there?

00:26:24.999 --> 00:26:26.296
How do you mean?

00:26:26.334 --> 00:26:28.063
An altercation perhaps?

00:26:28.102 --> 00:26:30.627
Possibly involving
Lieutenant Kwan.

00:26:30.672 --> 00:26:32.367
No, nothing like that.

00:26:32.407 --> 00:26:35.376
The way I remember it,
things went pretty smoothly.

00:26:35.410 --> 00:26:38.436
What's this all about,
if you don't mind my asking?

00:26:38.479 --> 00:26:39.969
Not at all.

00:26:40.014 --> 00:26:43.882
When I was in the nacelle room,
I had an empathic experience.

00:26:43.918 --> 00:26:46.887
We believe the Counselor
may have been seeing

00:26:46.955 --> 00:26:49.549
an event that occurred
eight years ago.

00:26:49.591 --> 00:26:51.252
And I saw you there.

00:26:51.292 --> 00:26:54.557
Do you have any idea
why that might be?

00:26:54.596 --> 00:26:56.029
I'm afraid I don't.

00:26:56.064 --> 00:26:57.895
Lieutenant, are you aware

00:26:57.932 --> 00:27:01.561
that I can sense when
someone's telling the truth?

00:27:01.603 --> 00:27:03.127
I've heard that.

00:27:03.171 --> 00:27:05.605
Then, I'm sure that
if you remember anything

00:27:05.640 --> 00:27:07.699
that might be relevant
to our investigation

00:27:07.742 --> 00:27:09.073
you'll contact me.

00:27:09.110 --> 00:27:11.044
Oh, of course.

00:27:11.079 --> 00:27:13.775
Thank you, Lieutenant.

00:27:13.815 --> 00:27:15.214
Counselor.

00:27:21.322 --> 00:27:22.755
The strange thing is

00:27:22.790 --> 00:27:24.690
I couldn't read him at all.

00:27:24.726 --> 00:27:26.193
But you implied that...

00:27:26.227 --> 00:27:28.559
We have played poker many times.

00:27:28.596 --> 00:27:30.791
I've never known you to bluff.

00:27:30.832 --> 00:27:33.027
Well, it wouldn't be
much of a bluff

00:27:33.067 --> 00:27:34.864
if you knew, would it?

00:27:34.936 --> 00:27:37.234
The fact
that I couldn't read him

00:27:37.272 --> 00:27:40.002
suggests that he has at least
some telepathic ability.

00:27:40.041 --> 00:27:41.531
But Pierce is human.

00:27:41.576 --> 00:27:43.669
That's what I don't understand.

00:27:43.711 --> 00:27:45.872
Even though I couldn't
read his emotions

00:27:45.947 --> 00:27:48.381
I did feel that he was
holding something back.

00:27:48.416 --> 00:27:50.714
I thought so, as well.

00:27:50.752 --> 00:27:52.583
Maybe we should try to access

00:27:52.620 --> 00:27:55.111
the engineering logs
from Utopia Planitia.

00:27:55.156 --> 00:27:57.249
We might find out
more about him.

00:27:57.292 --> 00:28:00.420
There may be something in them
about Lieutenant Kwan, as well.

00:28:00.461 --> 00:28:01.655
Mm-hmm.

00:28:14.108 --> 00:28:17.475
It's going to take
about half an hour

00:28:17.512 --> 00:28:19.844
for the transmission
to be completed.

00:28:19.881 --> 00:28:23.647
Perhaps we should continue this
in the morning.

00:28:23.685 --> 00:28:26.051
It is late.

00:28:26.087 --> 00:28:29.454
Yes, and you must be tired.

00:28:29.490 --> 00:28:31.048
A little.

00:28:31.092 --> 00:28:34.858
So, I will say good night.

00:28:34.929 --> 00:28:36.920
Good night.

00:28:40.101 --> 00:28:43.002
We should get
an early start tomorrow.

00:28:43.037 --> 00:28:45.528
I think we should.

00:28:45.573 --> 00:28:48.235
I'll see you in the morning.

00:28:48.276 --> 00:28:50.244
Yes.

00:29:55.909 --> 00:29:57.206
Hello.

00:29:57.243 --> 00:29:59.404
Breakfast is ready.

00:29:59.445 --> 00:30:04.314
That sounds nice,
but it can wait.

00:30:09.255 --> 00:30:12.281
Why didn't we do this
a long time ago?

00:30:12.325 --> 00:30:15.692
Crusher to Counselor Troi.

00:30:15.728 --> 00:30:18.060
Yes, Doctor?

00:30:18.097 --> 00:30:19.496
I've synthesized the inhibitor.

00:30:19.532 --> 00:30:21.625
Please come to Sick Bay
whenever you're ready.

00:30:21.668 --> 00:30:23.295
Acknowledged.

00:30:26.039 --> 00:30:28.405
Crusher to Lieutenant Worf.

00:30:28.441 --> 00:30:30.238
Worf here.

00:30:30.276 --> 00:30:32.301
Medical supplies are ready

00:30:32.345 --> 00:30:35.007
to be taken
to cargo bay for transport.

00:30:35.048 --> 00:30:37.448
I will be there shortly.

00:30:42.789 --> 00:30:45.587
This should take effect
immediately.

00:30:45.625 --> 00:30:49.061
Will it completely suppress
my empathic abilities?

00:30:49.095 --> 00:30:50.926
It's hard to say for sure

00:30:50.964 --> 00:30:53.592
but I can always
increase the dosage

00:30:53.633 --> 00:30:55.066
if it's not enough.

00:30:55.101 --> 00:31:00.038
The cargo bay will be off limits
to all but medical personnel.

00:31:00.073 --> 00:31:01.938
Thanks for your help, sir.

00:31:01.975 --> 00:31:03.875
You're welcome.

00:31:03.910 --> 00:31:05.537
Good morning.

00:31:05.578 --> 00:31:07.307
Counselor.

00:31:07.347 --> 00:31:10.475
Data and Geordi are already
in the nacelle tube.

00:31:10.516 --> 00:31:11.540
Are you ready?

00:31:11.584 --> 00:31:13.142
Yes.

00:31:14.620 --> 00:31:16.349
Excuse me, sir.

00:31:16.389 --> 00:31:18.550
About the quarantine field
in the cargo bay?

00:31:18.591 --> 00:31:21.151
It looks like we'll need
a second field generator.

00:31:22.895 --> 00:31:23.884
I am needed here.

00:31:23.930 --> 00:31:25.329
I will join you
as soon as I can.

00:31:25.365 --> 00:31:26.593
All right.

00:31:26.632 --> 00:31:30.068
Apparently my help
was not so good after all.

00:31:30.103 --> 00:31:32.196
Yes, it was.

00:31:32.238 --> 00:31:33.398
You were wonderful.

00:31:33.439 --> 00:31:34.804
I think I know what is wrong.

00:31:34.841 --> 00:31:36.240
The generator dispersion...

00:31:46.452 --> 00:31:48.716
Counselor

00:31:48.755 --> 00:31:49.915
are you okay?

00:31:49.956 --> 00:31:50.923
I'm fine.

00:31:51.024 --> 00:31:53.390
The inhibitor seems
to be working.

00:31:53.426 --> 00:31:55.553
Have you found anything?

00:31:55.595 --> 00:31:58.462
No, nothing unusual.

00:32:05.571 --> 00:32:08.631
I don't remember seeing these
during my empathic experience.

00:32:08.674 --> 00:32:10.972
Have they been here
since the ship was built?

00:32:11.010 --> 00:32:13.069
No, they were installed
two years ago.

00:32:21.988 --> 00:32:23.979
Geordi...

00:32:25.858 --> 00:32:30.454
I remember seeing a plasma
conduit right there.

00:32:30.496 --> 00:32:34.057
The main ODN line runs
right behind that panel.

00:32:34.100 --> 00:32:36.068
It lifts out,
so you can get to it.

00:32:36.102 --> 00:32:39.868
Kwan was working on that conduit
the day before he died.

00:32:39.906 --> 00:32:41.430
Can you open it?

00:32:41.474 --> 00:32:43.840
Sure, it'll take just a minute.

00:32:49.348 --> 00:32:51.339
Data.

00:33:06.466 --> 00:33:10.869
Lieutenant Nara,
may I ask you something?

00:33:10.903 --> 00:33:12.564
The work Lieutenant Kwan

00:33:12.605 --> 00:33:14.869
was doing...
was it unusual in any way?

00:33:14.941 --> 00:33:18.570
He was refitting a field coil

00:33:18.611 --> 00:33:20.238
but it was
probably the first time

00:33:20.279 --> 00:33:21.974
that particular panel's
been opened

00:33:22.014 --> 00:33:23.276
since the ship was built.

00:33:23.316 --> 00:33:25.284
Thank you.

00:33:34.393 --> 00:33:36.361
No!

00:33:41.000 --> 00:33:43.764
Counselor?

00:33:43.803 --> 00:33:45.600
Are you all right?

00:33:45.638 --> 00:33:49.734
Something happened
when you removed the panel.

00:33:49.775 --> 00:33:52.209
There's something in there.

00:33:59.285 --> 00:34:02.118
I am getting readings
that indicate organic material

00:34:02.155 --> 00:34:04.089
embedded in this wall.

00:34:04.123 --> 00:34:05.112
Organic?

00:34:06.559 --> 00:34:07.526
You're right.

00:34:07.560 --> 00:34:09.221
Let me reconfigure
the emitter beam.

00:34:09.262 --> 00:34:10.854
We might be able
to see what it is.

00:34:10.930 --> 00:34:12.522
There.

00:34:24.577 --> 00:34:28.240
This dosage should prevent
any further empathic flashes.

00:34:31.250 --> 00:34:33.548
The bone fragments
are definitely human.

00:34:33.586 --> 00:34:35.486
I sequenced a DNA sample.

00:34:35.521 --> 00:34:37.955
I'll see if I can match it
to Starfleet records.

00:34:42.195 --> 00:34:45.392
Accessing Starfleet
personnel records.

00:34:45.431 --> 00:34:47.262
I'd say these fragments
have been in the wall

00:34:47.300 --> 00:34:48.392
about seven or eight years.

00:34:48.434 --> 00:34:50.493
...your help with the Barson
medical supplies.

00:34:50.536 --> 00:34:51.696
Your handling of the...

00:34:51.737 --> 00:34:54.228
You said something happened
when the panel was opened.

00:34:54.273 --> 00:34:55.240
Yes.

00:34:55.274 --> 00:34:56.400
I wonder if these fragments

00:34:56.442 --> 00:34:59.343
could have somehow
triggered your experience?

00:34:59.378 --> 00:35:02.541
I'll run a resonance scan,
see if anything turns up.

00:35:02.582 --> 00:35:05.050
Sir, I think
we've found a match.

00:35:07.086 --> 00:35:08.781
Apparently, the remains

00:35:08.821 --> 00:35:11.085
are those
of an Ensign Marla Finn.

00:35:11.123 --> 00:35:13.591
I'm trying to find
a picture of her in the records.

00:35:15.027 --> 00:35:17.552
That's her.

00:35:17.597 --> 00:35:19.861
That's the woman I saw.

00:35:23.436 --> 00:35:25.870
It says she was
reported missing

00:35:25.938 --> 00:35:30.602
"from Utopia Planitia
on Stardate 40987.2."

00:35:30.643 --> 00:35:32.543
Eight years ago.

00:35:32.578 --> 00:35:36.480
But how did her body
become embedded in a bulkhead?

00:35:36.515 --> 00:35:39.109
Maybe there was some kind
of an accident.

00:35:39.151 --> 00:35:40.118
Or she was killed

00:35:40.152 --> 00:35:41.983
and the murderer
hid her remains.

00:35:42.021 --> 00:35:44.615
Something's not right.

00:35:44.657 --> 00:35:48.149
Pull up Lieutenant Kwan's
service record.

00:35:49.562 --> 00:35:51.427
I thought so.

00:35:51.464 --> 00:35:53.295
He didn't arrive at the shipyard

00:35:53.332 --> 00:35:55.323
until six months
after Finn's death.

00:35:55.368 --> 00:35:57.893
I couldn't have been seeing
through his eyes.

00:35:57.970 --> 00:35:59.562
Then whose?

00:35:59.605 --> 00:36:01.038
Well, it would have
to be someone

00:36:01.073 --> 00:36:02.700
who was at least
partially telepathic.

00:36:02.742 --> 00:36:04.073
Pierce.

00:36:04.110 --> 00:36:05.737
But you saw him there.

00:36:05.778 --> 00:36:10.078
Yes, but not as clearly
as I could see everything else.

00:36:10.116 --> 00:36:11.811
His face looked...

00:36:11.851 --> 00:36:14.217
like that.

00:36:14.253 --> 00:36:15.743
A reflection.

00:36:15.788 --> 00:36:18.416
So I was seeing
through his eyes.

00:36:18.457 --> 00:36:21.790
And Finn was trying
to get away from him.

00:36:21.827 --> 00:36:24.057
She was afraid of him.

00:36:24.096 --> 00:36:25.620
I think it is time

00:36:25.665 --> 00:36:30.068
we had another conversation
with Lieutenant Pierce.

00:36:30.102 --> 00:36:31.660
Ensign Calloway...

00:36:32.972 --> 00:36:34.496
thank you for your help.

00:37:07.506 --> 00:37:09.474
Deck ten.

00:37:09.508 --> 00:37:11.840
Worf, can I ask you something?

00:37:11.944 --> 00:37:15.141
Do you regret
what happened last night?

00:37:15.181 --> 00:37:17.513
No. No, of course not.

00:37:17.550 --> 00:37:19.142
Are you sure?
Because I don't want

00:37:19.185 --> 00:37:20.174
to jeopardize our friendship.

00:37:20.219 --> 00:37:24.713
Deanna, I do not regret
being with you.

00:37:27.727 --> 00:37:29.194
What is wrong?

00:37:33.032 --> 00:37:35.660
I'm not... feeling myself.

00:37:35.701 --> 00:37:37.100
Maybe it's the inhibitor.

00:37:37.136 --> 00:37:39.730
I'm so used to sensing
what people are feeling

00:37:39.772 --> 00:37:41.740
and now I can't.

00:37:41.774 --> 00:37:45.710
Perhaps I should talk
to Lieutenant Pierce alone.

00:37:45.745 --> 00:37:47.337
That might be a good idea.

00:37:47.380 --> 00:37:50.247
I will meet you
in your quarters later.

00:37:50.282 --> 00:37:53.115
I'll be waiting for you.

00:37:59.959 --> 00:38:01.927
Deck eight.

00:38:14.173 --> 00:38:15.538
Come in.

00:38:31.056 --> 00:38:33.524
Security
to Counselor Troi's quarters.

00:38:33.559 --> 00:38:34.548
Acknowledged.

00:38:34.593 --> 00:38:35.753
I don't understand.

00:38:35.794 --> 00:38:38.160
Lieutenant Worf said you wanted
to talk to me about something.

00:38:38.197 --> 00:38:40.427
Where is he?

00:38:40.466 --> 00:38:42.866
He said he had to go somewhere.

00:38:42.901 --> 00:38:45.233
Troi to Worf.

00:38:46.972 --> 00:38:49.668
Computer,
where is Lieutenant Worf?

00:38:49.708 --> 00:38:54.304
Lieutenant Worf is
in Ensign Calloway's quarters.

00:38:57.082 --> 00:38:58.049
Counselor?

00:38:58.083 --> 00:38:59.448
Take Lieutenant Pierce
to his quarters

00:38:59.485 --> 00:39:01.146
and hold him there.

00:39:23.809 --> 00:39:25.674
Security override.

00:39:25.711 --> 00:39:28.305
Authorization:
Troi-delta-two-nine.

00:39:38.724 --> 00:39:41.693
Stop it.

00:39:46.799 --> 00:39:48.562
Stop it!

00:39:49.568 --> 00:39:51.502
Stop it!

00:40:07.119 --> 00:40:08.746
He's dead.

00:40:08.787 --> 00:40:10.414
You killed him!

00:40:10.455 --> 00:40:11.854
No!

00:40:23.335 --> 00:40:25.303
You know what you have to do.

00:41:10.983 --> 00:41:15.317
I know what I have to do.

00:41:19.358 --> 00:41:20.552
Warning.

00:41:20.592 --> 00:41:21.650
What are you doing?

00:41:21.693 --> 00:41:24.184
Plasma venting system
will engage in 70 seconds.

00:41:24.229 --> 00:41:25.719
You're alive.

00:41:25.764 --> 00:41:27.755
You're all right.

00:41:41.580 --> 00:41:44.777
I opened the maintenance door
at Counselor Troi's request.

00:41:44.816 --> 00:41:47.751
Then turned to see her standing
too close to the force field.

00:41:47.786 --> 00:41:49.219
It all seemed so real to me.

00:41:49.254 --> 00:41:51.552
I can't believe
that everything I experienced

00:41:51.590 --> 00:41:53.353
happened
in just those few seconds.

00:41:53.392 --> 00:41:56.691
It appears Counselor Troi
was correct.

00:41:56.728 --> 00:41:59.891
Pierce was
partially telepathic.

00:41:59.932 --> 00:42:03.197
His maternal grandmother
was born on Betazed.

00:42:03.235 --> 00:42:04.793
What else have you found out?

00:42:04.836 --> 00:42:06.463
According to Starfleet records

00:42:06.505 --> 00:42:09.736
Pierce and the other persons
Counselor Troi identified

00:42:09.775 --> 00:42:12.437
were killed in an accidental
plasma discharge

00:42:12.477 --> 00:42:13.444
eight years ago.

00:42:13.478 --> 00:42:15.571
Their bodies were never found.

00:42:15.614 --> 00:42:17.809
I don't believe
it was an accident.

00:42:17.849 --> 00:42:18.838
I think Lieutenant Pierce

00:42:18.884 --> 00:42:20.784
found out the other two
were having an affair.

00:42:20.819 --> 00:42:24.016
He lost control
and he killed them both.

00:42:24.056 --> 00:42:26.524
Afterwards, he probably
activated the plasma stream

00:42:26.558 --> 00:42:28.355
and then threw himself into it.

00:42:28.393 --> 00:42:30.588
The plasma discharge
would have obliterated

00:42:30.629 --> 00:42:32.290
any evidence that it was murder.

00:42:36.535 --> 00:42:40.767
I scanned behind the panel
Counselor Troi asked me to.

00:42:40.806 --> 00:42:43.366
I didn't find any bone fragments

00:42:43.408 --> 00:42:46.741
but I did find some traces
of cellular residue.

00:42:46.778 --> 00:42:49.906
It's showing some kind
of psionic signature.

00:42:49.982 --> 00:42:51.916
It may be that
when Lieutenant Pierce

00:42:52.017 --> 00:42:53.882
was struck by the plasma stream

00:42:53.919 --> 00:42:55.887
the subspace energy
present there

00:42:55.921 --> 00:42:59.084
imprinted his empathic pattern
into the residue.

00:42:59.124 --> 00:43:01.854
Kind of like
a psychic photograph.

00:43:01.893 --> 00:43:04.589
That's what triggered
my hallucination.

00:43:04.629 --> 00:43:07.860
My mind must have taken
elements from my own life

00:43:07.933 --> 00:43:10.163
and then created a situation
that, in many ways, mirrored

00:43:10.202 --> 00:43:12.898
what happened to Pierce.

00:43:15.374 --> 00:43:18.104
If you hadn't been there

00:43:18.143 --> 00:43:20.634
I would have jumped
just like he did.

00:43:29.554 --> 00:43:31.419
Counselor.

00:43:35.427 --> 00:43:38.396
When I pulled you
from the plasma stream

00:43:38.430 --> 00:43:40.261
you seemed...

00:43:40.298 --> 00:43:42.732
surprised I was alive.

00:43:42.768 --> 00:43:44.599
Well, actually...

00:43:44.636 --> 00:43:48.094
in my hallucination,
you were killed.

00:43:48.140 --> 00:43:50.904
May I ask by whom?

00:43:50.976 --> 00:43:53.843
Well, you know
what they say, Mr. Worf.

00:43:53.879 --> 00:43:57.474
Hell hath no fury
like a woman scorned.
